{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And the reason for <b>lest they teach you to do according to all their abominations, which they have done for their gods</b>, is that they might teach you to serve the honored Name by burning your sons and your daughters, and every abomination of HaShem that He hates, so that you would sin against HaShem your Elohim — for He warned you lest you say, \"How do these nations serve their gods? I will do likewise\" (Deuteronomy 12:30). Now, the Torah already warned (Exodus 23:33), \"They shall not dwell in your land, lest they cause you to sin against Me, for you will serve their gods, for it will be a snare to you\" — and this is a warning against idolatry, for if you make a covenant with them and with their gods, they will dwell in your land, and many among them will entice you to serve idolatry. And here He added to explain, \"you shall not let any soul live,\" for even a single individual remaining among you who serves you will recall to you the worship of their gods, and perhaps you will be enticed to do the same for the honored Name, and you will sin before Him, may He be blessed."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:52:15.606906151Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}